 ### [Fixed-rate Block-coding (VTC/S3TC)](5727-fixed-rate-block-coding-vtc-s3tc.md)
-Extends 2D S3TC to 3D volumes with hardware acceleration.
+Extends 2D S3TC to 3D volumes with hardware acceleration. It solves the problem of storing large volumetric datasets in limited GPU memory by approximating voxel values through linear interpolation from a small set of representative values. It is chosen when real-time rendering without decompressing the entire volume into RAM is required. It is distinct from its sibling(52-s3tc.md) by its native support for 3D textures.
 
 ### [Uniform Quantization](5855-uniform-quantization.md)
-Maps values to equally spaced levels across the entire dataset range.
+Maps values to equally spaced levels across the entire dataset range. It is chosen for simplicity and predictable compression ratios, typically achieving 4:1 compression by representing 32-bit floats with 8-bit integers. It differs from [Non-uniform Quantization](5858-non-uniform-quantization.md) by using fixed-width intervals for all levels, which makes it simple to implement but prone to losing features in data with wide dynamic ranges.
 
